Fillets: a rounding that ends where its edge runs on tangentially into an
edge not rounded, the face at the end going on tangentially from one of
the rounding's faces, ends where that face's surface, followed back along
the rounding, cuts it across (mitcad#422).

The case: a thread's crest (the edge between the post's cylinder and the
groove's lower flank) rounded down to the thread's run-out, a straight cut
whose lower flank is the plane tangent to the groove's flank along the
start profile. At the run-out the crest runs on into the run-out's crest,
not rounded; the end is OnSame, the face at the end being the run-out's
flank. Its plane only touches the rounding near the vertex, and OCCT's
corner there cut the rounding by that touch, the rounding running on down
to the run-out with a small corner patch. The bodies the `.ipt` files
store end such a rounding where the plane cuts it across a turn back (331
degrees up the crest, where the crest rises out of the plane again): a face
of 0.006 mm2 on the plane closes it there and the crest stays sharp from
there down to the run-out.

- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformCapAtTangentEndFace (called before the other
  ends of a lone stripe at a vertex of three edges): where the end is
  OnSame and the face at the end goes on tangentially (G1, across an edge
  at the vertex) from a face of the spine's edge, each contact is followed
  back from the end, sampled every quarter of the radius, to where it first
  passes from the side of that face's solid of its surface to the outside
  (bisected). Where both contacts do so on one surfdata, more than four
  radii from the vertex, the blend ends there: the surfdatas past the cut
  are dropped, the last one ends on the curve where the surface cuts it
  (ChFi3d_ComputeCurves), and a corner stripe on that surface (its normal
  turned to the outside as the blend's is) closes the end, between the cut
  and the point Q where the surface crosses the spine's edge, along its
  intersection curves with the blend's two faces, ending in Q, where the
  spine's edge is cut. The spine's end becomes a free one (no corner at the
  vertex). Elsewhere nothing changes.
